Parent: 1468

## Context and scope

Implementation child of red-main tracker 1468. Its sole criterion is an
actual after-merge record, which cannot exist before the merge producing it.
The advisor recommended this decomposition rather than weakening that
criterion. Existing implementation commit 3e7a80b0 and evidence commit
23b2af8c are inherited on PR #2267; no new implementation scope is added.

Repair only the three stale memory assertions identified by 1468. Preserve
the author-reviewed memory prose and useful behavioral checks. The original
three assertion failures were reproduced; affected modules have 20 passing
checks, with an injected-index sensitivity control in both runtime contexts.

## Relevant files

- tests/test_dream_v8.py
- tests/test_memory_v8_pilot.py
- tests/test_on_start_memory_injection.py

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Remove obsolete supersession wording and universal inventory-filename
  assertions without restoring prose the author removed.
- [ ] Retain structural checks that each topic cites an existing source
  outside the topic directory.
- [ ] Non-injection coverage derives from the current nonempty index, checks
  successful hook execution and nonempty output, and rejects injected index
  text in both repository and no-project contexts.
- [ ] Affected test modules and required before-merge checks pass on the
  candidate; review shows no production or memory-prose change.

The real full after-merge record remains required by parent 1468. This child
neither asserts that future record already exists nor closes the parent.
